"How can a computer seem to do several things at once when the processor does one thing at a time?": "2e851e26cac1",
"Most programs finish a task and stop. An operating system keeps running until the computer is turned off. The first computers had none: they ran one program at a time, and a human operator looked after everything else. Today many computers have several processor cores, so a few things really can happen at the same moment. But there are usually many more programs than cores, so taking turns is still how it works.": "d0bf4239aac3",
